IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`
IMPORT `g3-art10-public-access`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-art10-public-access.l4: tests of Article 10 (src:287-297).  Expected values are decided from the text before the code was run.

§ `Tests of Article 10: public access`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

§§ `Article 10(1) and 10(2): the duty and the power`

-- No time is stated for 10(1): the duty stands until performed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 10(1) the Commissioner must make the public parts of the register available on a website` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge` AT 30

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST `make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge`
#TRACE `Art 10(1) the Commissioner must make the public parts of the register available on a website` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- 10(2): a permission of the Minister.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 10(2) the Minister may by Order provide for other access to the public parts of the register` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order prescribing` `another manner in which the public parts of the register are made available, on payment of a charge` AT 12

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MAY `make an Order prescribing`
#TRACE `Art 10(2) the Minister may by Order provide for other access to the public parts of the register` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

GIVEN manner IS A BOOLEAN
      charge IS A MAYBE `Charge for access to the public parts of the register (Article 10(2))`
GIVETH A `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)`
`an Order for another manner` manner `, requiring` charge MEANS
    `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)` WITH
        `specifies another manner in which the public parts are made available` IS manner
        `payment required` IS charge

-- On payment of (a) a specified charge, or (b) a charge determined and published by the Commissioner.
#ASSERT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` (JUST `a specified charge`))
#ASSERT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` (JUST `a charge determined and published by the Commissioner`))
-- Without payment, or without a specified manner, it is not an Order Article 10(2) reaches.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`an Order for another manner` FALSE `, requiring` (JUST `a specified charge`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`an Order for another manner` FALSE `, requiring` NOTHING)
-- The paragraphs one by one.
#ASSERT `Art 10(2)(a) the Order requires payment of a specified charge` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` (JUST `a specified charge`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(2)(a) the Order requires payment of a specified charge` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` (JUST `a charge determined and published by the Commissioner`))
#ASSERT `Art 10(2)(b) the Order requires payment of a charge determined and published by the Commissioner` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` (JUST `a charge determined and published by the Commissioner`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(2)(b) the Order requires payment of a charge determined and published by the Commissioner` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` (JUST `a specified charge`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(2)(b) the Order requires payment of a charge determined and published by the Commissioner` (`an Order for another manner` TRUE `, requiring` NOTHING)

§§ `Article 10(3): which parts of the register are public`

`a company, not on the register` MEANS `an entity called` "Nobody Yet" `standing as` `not on the register` `and falling within` (LIST `a company`)

GIVEN e IS AN Entity
      m IS A `Matter entered on the register`
      designated IS A BOOLEAN
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`public, asked of` e `about the matter` m `designation made` designated `on the readings` interp MEANS
    `Art 10(3) the matter is in a public part of the register` interp e m designated

`item 8(3)` MEANS `an item required by Article 8(3)`
`item 8(5)` MEANS `an item required by Article 8(5)`

-- (a) The general section: everything entered is public, the name included.
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` `the registered name` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` `the registration number` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- (b) The restricted section: only the public elements -- the number, not the name; the five matters of 9(1)(b); not the governors, the address, the date, the notes of (h), (i), (l), (m), (n).
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` `the registration number` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` `the registered name` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `a note of the status of the entity`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the registered charitable purposes`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the registered public benefit statement`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the date on which the charity was registered`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` `the summary of the reasons for registration, produced by the charity` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` `another element prescribed by an Order under Article 9(1)(d)` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- (c) The historic section: everything, the name included.
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `about the matter` `the registered name` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `about the matter` (`item 8(5)` `the entity's former registered number`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `about the matter` (`item 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `about the matter` (`item 8(5)` `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- An entity in no section has nothing in a public part.
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company, not on the register` `about the matter` `the registration number` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company that applies` `about the matter` `the registered name` `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav

-- Subject to paragraph (5): a designated matter of a registered charity is not public.
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) `designation made` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `about the matter` `the registration number` `designation made` TRUE `on the readings` fav
-- A designation is of one matter: the others stay public.
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`) `designation made` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- F3.3: the Commissioner cannot designate a matter in the historic section on the reading taken, so a purported designation leaves it public; on the other reading it is not public.
#ASSERT `public, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `about the matter` (`item 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`) `designation made` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `about the matter` (`item 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`) `designation made` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.3 reading B`
-- Not disturbed: the designation of a registered charity's matter is effective on both readings.
#ASSERT NOT `public, asked of` `a company in the general section` `about the matter` (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) `designation made` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.3 reading B`

§§ `Article 10(4) and (5): the Commissioner's designation`

GIVEN e IS AN Entity
      risk IS A BOOLEAN
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (5) applies to` e `with the risk considered` risk `on the readings` interp MEANS
    `Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` interp e risk

-- The Commissioner must consider that safety or security would be significantly put at risk: no consideration, no power.
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company in the general section` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company in the restricted section` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company in the general section` `with the risk considered` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company in the restricted section` `with the risk considered` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- A registered charity only (F3.3 A): not an applicant, not an entity in no section, not a deregistered entity.
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company, formerly registered` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company that applies` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company, not on the register` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` fav
-- F3.3 B: a formerly registered charity is a "registered charity" for this paragraph.
#ASSERT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company, formerly registered` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.3 reading B`
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company, formerly registered` `with the risk considered` FALSE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.3 reading B`
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company that applies` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.3 reading B`
#ASSERT NOT `paragraph (5) applies to` `a company, not on the register` `with the risk considered` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.3 reading B`

-- The power: where paragraph (5) applies, the Commissioner may designate the matter; exercised or not, no breach.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 10(5) the Commissioner may designate the matter as not a public part of the register` fav `a company in the general section` TRUE (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `designate a matter as not being a public part of the register` (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) AT 10

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MAY `designate a matter as not being a public part of the register`
#TRACE `Art 10(5) the Commissioner may designate the matter as not a public part of the register` fav `a company in the general section` TRUE (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- No power where the risk is not considered: nothing is owed and nothing is open.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 10(5) the Commissioner may designate the matter as not a public part of the register` fav `a company in the general section` FALSE (`item 8(3)` `the principal address`) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- A deregistered entity on the favoured reading: no power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 10(5) the Commissioner may designate the matter as not a public part of the register` fav `a company, formerly registered` TRUE (`item 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- ... and on the other reading it stands as a power.
-- EXPECT: STANDING | MAY `designate a matter as not being a public part of the register`
#TRACE `Art 10(5) the Commissioner may designate the matter as not a public part of the register` `interpretation F3.3 reading B` `a company, formerly registered` TRUE (`item 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
